<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Jagiellon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1461–1506</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Jagiellon was grand duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from 1492 and king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> from 1501 until his death in 1506, a son of Casimir IV. He married Helena, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, but could not prevent Muscovite conquests, including the defeat at Vedrosha in 1500. In 1505 he accepted the Nihil novi constitution, which strengthened the Polish parliament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-jagiellon.jpg" alt="Alexander Jagiellon" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Goraj · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goraj_Miracle_of_Saint_Simeon_Stylites_(detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
